From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:51:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 116/116] LOCAL: arm64: configs: nairo: Build in dispcc

Without clk_ignore_unused, clocks that are on but not claimed are
switched off at late_initcall_sync. The bootloader splash is kept
alive by simpledrm, which holds the GCC display clocks and the MDSS
GDSC, but simpledrm can only probe once the display clock controller
is there. As a module, the controller loads from the root filesystem
seconds later, after the GCC display clocks have been switched off.

Build the display clock controller in, so that simpledrm probes
during the deferred probe flush at late_initcall and claims the
display clocks before unused clocks are disabled.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg

Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config b/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
index 6112580ed..da2b05681 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/nairo.config
@@ -81,3 +81,6 @@ CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_SM7250=y
 # Display panel
 CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_NOVATEK_NT36672C=m
 CONFIG_REGULATOR_QCOM_LCDB=m
+# Display clock controller built in: simpledrm must claim the display
+# clocks before unused clocks are switched off at late init
+CONFIG_SM_DISPCC_8250=y
